WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.927 --> 00:00:08.005
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

2
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.074
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

3
00:02:03.758 --> 00:02:05.958
Where are you going?
- I'll be right back.

4
00:03:30.538 --> 00:03:34.337
You shouldn't have brought them.
- But dad is out there.

5
00:03:55.733 --> 00:04:02.211
Take cover. Port. get ready to fire.
- Get ready to fire.

6
00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:05.411
Hard to starboard.

7
00:04:22.446 --> 00:04:24.246
Admiral Tromp is trapped.

8
00:04:26.006 --> 00:04:28.045
Square away the yards.

9
00:04:28.166 --> 00:04:31.285
Michiel. this is madness.
- Luff up to port.

10
00:04:31.404 --> 00:04:34.523
Luff up to port.

11
00:04:37.003 --> 00:04:39.123
We can't leave Tromp to die.

12
00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:54.399
Chop it.
Chuck that mast overboard. Chop.

13
00:05:11.515 --> 00:05:14.914
We'll push those idiot English
back to their island.

14
00:05:15.035 --> 00:05:17.554
Until death. admiral.
- Go straight.

15
00:05:17.673 --> 00:05:19.913
Mainsail halyard.

16
00:05:24.552 --> 00:05:28.031
To port.
- Get ready to tack.

17
00:05:31.911 --> 00:05:34.031
Get ready to fire.

18
00:06:22.338 --> 00:06:23.619
Michiel.

19
00:06:31.897 --> 00:06:33.456
Good work.

20
00:06:38.415 --> 00:06:40.255
The admiral...

21
00:06:46.972 --> 00:06:50.332
He's calling all captains.
Get a sloop ready.

22
00:06:50.451 --> 00:06:54.570
You want to row there?
- You. you and you jump in. come on.

23
00:07:19.966 --> 00:07:23.085
Michiel? You're just in time.

24
00:07:23.205 --> 00:07:26.763
You'll be all right.
-It's nothing.

25
00:07:28.203 --> 00:07:29.963
We'll get you to port.

26
00:07:30.082 --> 00:07:32.361
The wind is blowing the wrong way.

27
00:07:33.762 --> 00:07:38.320
Like politicians. very unpredictable.

28
00:07:38.441 --> 00:07:39.641
Don't talk.

29
00:07:39.761 --> 00:07:43.559
My men need someone like you.

30
00:07:44.959 --> 00:07:47.278
Someone who keeps his course.

31
00:07:48.278 --> 00:07:51.637
You can do it.

32
00:07:51.757 --> 00:07:53.197
Michiel.

33
00:08:11.593 --> 00:08:13.232
Go and help people.

34
00:08:23.630 --> 00:08:25.231
Are you all right?
- Yes.

35
00:08:25.351 --> 00:08:27.709
This morning you also...
- I'm fine.

36
00:09:01.902 --> 00:09:07.221
The new prime minister
of Holland and West Friesland.

37
00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:13.659
The right honourable lord Johan de Witt.

38
00:09:15.579 --> 00:09:17.539
Thank you.

39
00:09:17.658 --> 00:09:19.898
As regent of the Prince of Orange...

40
00:09:20.018 --> 00:09:22.777
I think I speak on behalf
of all members...

41
00:09:22.896 --> 00:09:27.096
when I say we're glad with
our new chairman from mighty Holland.

42
00:09:30.174 --> 00:09:32.535
Some would say relieved.

43
00:09:33.533 --> 00:09:37.333
I. for one. will sleep better
now we have a man at the helm...

44
00:09:37.454 --> 00:09:40.692
who'll serve the interests
of all the provinces.

45
00:09:40.812 --> 00:09:43.812
And not just those
of his republican friends.

46
00:09:44.731 --> 00:09:50.090
I presume lord Kievit
can rise above the parties.

47
00:09:51.131 --> 00:09:53.650
I was thinking
of the Prince of Orange.

48
00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:59.168
How can the Prince
rise above the parties...

49
00:09:59.289 --> 00:10:01.727
when he doesn't even reach my belt?

50
00:10:05.288 --> 00:10:08.127
Order.

51
00:10:08.886 --> 00:10:12.126
We will hear the honourable De Witt.

52
00:10:14.124 --> 00:10:18.604
First. I'm very happy that lord Kievit
is sleeping well.

53
00:10:19.723 --> 00:10:25.883
To answer your question:
I understand your concerns. I do.

54
00:10:26.002 --> 00:10:30.521
There is no one in this country who
understands you more than I do.

55
00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:38.720
My father was imprisoned
for disagreeing with the Orangists.

56
00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:42.759
I found out what it means
to live in a country...

57
00:10:42.878 --> 00:10:45.638
where you cannot say
what you are thinking.

58
00:10:45.757 --> 00:10:49.197
Do you want to live in such a country?
I don't.

59
00:10:49.318 --> 00:10:51.276
I don't think you do. either.

60
00:10:52.677 --> 00:10:57.235
Let me pose you a question.
We're a nation of merchants.

61
00:10:57.355 --> 00:11:02.155
We sail the seas of the world
with 20.000 ships.

62
00:11:02.274 --> 00:11:04.314
In trade. we all work together.

63
00:11:04.433 --> 00:11:07.513
To get better prices
and to help each other.

64
00:11:08.713 --> 00:11:12.152
And what do you think?
Does this work or not?

65
00:11:12.752 --> 00:11:16.990
It does. Some members became so
successful they hardly fit in the benches.

66
00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:22.828
When you do business
in the East or the West...

67
00:11:22.948 --> 00:11:26.988
do you do so
as Orangists or as republicans?

68
00:11:27.109 --> 00:11:30.908
And why are the English trying
to block our shipping routes?

69
00:11:31.067 --> 00:11:35.706
To disrupt trade. Is that because
you're an Orangist or a republican?

70
00:11:35.867 --> 00:11:40.344
No. the English want to wage war
against us. because we're Dutch.

71
00:11:40.506 --> 00:11:41.866
Free Dutchmen.

72
00:11:46.623 --> 00:11:49.822
Large monarchies consider
our small nation too rich.

73
00:11:49.943 --> 00:11:55.021
Too successful and too free.
On top of that. we're a republic.

74
00:11:55.622 --> 00:11:59.381
In which all men are free
to live their own lives.

75
00:11:59.501 --> 00:12:01.821
We decide how we worship God.

76
00:12:01.940 --> 00:12:04.499
No leader is more important
than the country itself.

77
00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:09.539
The English begrudge us our freedom.
Our freedom frightens them.

78
00:12:09.659 --> 00:12:14.737
Because we're prepared
to die for our freedom.

79
00:12:14.858 --> 00:12:19.297
Because we paid for our freedom
with our own blood.

80
00:12:19.416 --> 00:12:21.136
And I'm asking you:

81
00:12:21.255 --> 00:12:25.575
Haven't you all lost a relative
to the Spanish or the English?

82
00:12:25.734 --> 00:12:29.734
And was that republican blood
or Orangist blood?

83
00:12:29.855 --> 00:12:30.815
No.

84
00:12:31.774 --> 00:12:33.573
It was Dutch blood.

85
00:12:36.052 --> 00:12:37.892
It's our blood.

86
00:12:40.731 --> 00:12:42.092
This is our country.

87
00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:46.650
A country we conquered from the water.

88
00:12:46.771 --> 00:12:49.089
A country
where we earn our own happiness.

89
00:12:49.210 --> 00:12:52.529
By working hard.
in the villages and cities.

90
00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:54.608
In the ports and on the main land.

91
00:13:19.482 --> 00:13:24.242
Our freedom can only be protected if we are
willing to fight for freedom for others.

92
00:13:24.361 --> 00:13:30.480
That is why the Dutch lion
holds these seven arrows in his claw.

93
00:13:30.599 --> 00:13:32.160
That is what binds us.

94
00:13:40.159 --> 00:13:42.237
Your freedom is my freedom.

95
00:13:43.157 --> 00:13:46.356
I'll defend this freedom
until my last breath.

96
00:13:46.477 --> 00:13:49.475
Hear. hear.

97
00:14:19.549 --> 00:14:20.908
Gentlemen.

98
00:14:22.828 --> 00:14:25.148
Welcome home.
- Lord mayor.

99
00:14:46.023 --> 00:14:48.462
Leave it. Neeltje.
I can do it myself.

100
00:14:52.221 --> 00:14:53.821
I said...

101
00:15:06.217 --> 00:15:07.817
Sorry. I look awful.

102
00:15:15.616 --> 00:15:18.735
Why aren't you in bed?
- I'm feeling better.

103
00:15:44.769 --> 00:15:48.329
How long will you be staying?
- For as long as you like.

104
00:15:50.888 --> 00:15:52.288
Honestly?

105
00:15:54.528 --> 00:15:56.927
I've told them to find someone else.

106
00:15:57.846 --> 00:15:59.446
What about the English?

107
00:16:00.886 --> 00:16:02.445
They don't pay enough.

108
00:16:07.204 --> 00:16:09.804
The English will be quiet for a while.

109
00:16:14.603 --> 00:16:16.842
I want to get on with our lives.

110
00:16:21.320 --> 00:16:24.201
We can finally extend
the vegetable garden.

111
00:16:25.639 --> 00:16:27.641
Great... As much as you like.

112
00:16:29.839 --> 00:16:32.518
I'm glad I ordered
an extra cask of beer.

113
00:16:38.038 --> 00:16:40.316
All those lost years.

114
00:16:44.316 --> 00:16:47.234
You were on your own
because I was away.

115
00:16:50.795 --> 00:16:53.874
Was it a boy or a girl?
- A girl.

116
00:17:07.111 --> 00:17:09.309
I'm staying with you now.

117
00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:12.910
I won't abandon you anymore.

118
00:17:39.983 --> 00:17:42.983
Good morning.
- Slow down.

119
00:17:48.222 --> 00:17:51.061
Daddy.
- Sleepyhead.

120
00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:58.699
We're awake now.
- I couldn't stop them.

121
00:17:59.219 --> 00:18:01.898
You stink.
- Yes. of seaweed.

122
00:18:02.019 --> 00:18:05.418
Do I need a bath?
- There is a letter for you. daddy.

123
00:18:05.537 --> 00:18:08.136
What kind of letter?
- Come with us.

124
00:18:15.775 --> 00:18:17.134
Go ahead.

125
00:18:18.054 --> 00:18:19.414
Hello. son.

126
00:18:24.892 --> 00:18:26.973
There was a messenger.

127
00:18:27.092 --> 00:18:30.172
He had a fat horse.
- He came from The Hague.

128
00:18:30.291 --> 00:18:33.212
Open it.
- Michiel.

129
00:18:33.971 --> 00:18:36.410
We're not aboard a ship.

130
00:18:44.928 --> 00:18:46.847
Look. it has a little hole.

131
00:18:51.446 --> 00:18:53.527
10 copies from this one.

132
00:19:05.444 --> 00:19:06.803
Tromp?

133
00:19:24.759 --> 00:19:28.118
Mr De Ruyter?
This way. please.

134
00:19:43.994 --> 00:19:47.714
Mr De Ruyter. I've heard
so many good things about you.

135
00:19:47.834 --> 00:19:50.873
Really?
- You're the man to lead our fleet.

136
00:19:51.033 --> 00:19:53.873
You mean with Cornelis Tromp?
- No. under me.

137
00:19:53.992 --> 00:19:58.111
And not under Tromp?
- No. I want you. only you.

138
00:19:58.232 --> 00:20:00.191
As admiral?

139
00:20:00.311 --> 00:20:03.990
We need to rebuild
and modernize our fleet.

140
00:20:04.110 --> 00:20:06.149
I haven't served long enough.

141
00:20:06.270 --> 00:20:09.149
You have more experience than any other.
- As a sailor.

142
00:20:09.268 --> 00:20:12.029
No one will listen to me.
- We'll make them listen.

143
00:20:12.148 --> 00:20:14.907
I'm not of noble birth.
- Even better.

144
00:20:15.028 --> 00:20:17.187
Sailors are conservative.

145
00:20:17.307 --> 00:20:20.707
You can't just make anyone
admiral of the fleet.

146
00:20:20.826 --> 00:20:23.386
That's not how it works.
- Yes. it does.

147
00:20:23.466 --> 00:20:26.125
It's the 17th century.
anything is possible.

148
00:20:26.183 --> 00:20:27.482
This is ridiculous.

149
00:20:30.025 --> 00:20:32.144
You were raised as an Orangist.

150
00:20:32.265 --> 00:20:35.704
Most men in Zeeland were.
- I'm not into politics.

151
00:20:35.863 --> 00:20:39.823
But that is an advantage.
sailors have to trust their admiral.

152
00:20:42.061 --> 00:20:45.581
De Ruyter. this is in our nations interest.

153
00:20:46.062 --> 00:20:48.221
I'm not setting sail again.

154
00:20:50.021 --> 00:20:53.379
In the last 15 years.
I've spent six months at home.

155
00:20:54.499 --> 00:20:56.379
You have to find someone else.

156
00:20:57.579 --> 00:21:00.497
Are you serious?
- Didn't I make myself clear?

157
00:21:00.738 --> 00:21:04.576
I won't find a better man than you.
- Of course you will.

158
00:21:04.697 --> 00:21:08.615
This is the 17th century.
anything is possible. Gentlemen.

159
00:21:12.654 --> 00:21:14.174
What a strange fellow.

160
00:21:16.213 --> 00:21:18.053
What a strange fellow.

161
00:21:19.734 --> 00:21:21.933
I guess we'll make Sir Obdam admiral.

162
00:21:26.131 --> 00:21:28.291
Damn it. admiral. what must we do?

163
00:21:29.811 --> 00:21:31.730
Retreat.

164
00:21:34.968 --> 00:21:37.368
We've lost 25 ships.

165
00:21:38.849 --> 00:21:43.006
3000 dead and 2000 men
taken prisoner by the English.

166
00:21:43.366 --> 00:21:46.007
Good men.
who fought for their country.

167
00:21:48.486 --> 00:21:50.045
Honest men.

168
00:21:51.005 --> 00:21:54.484
Who trusted the prime minister.
- Hear. hear.

169
00:21:54.603 --> 00:21:57.604
Who trusted him with their lives.

170
00:21:59.043 --> 00:22:02.923
Order.
- Do you think this will be the end of it?

171
00:22:04.763 --> 00:22:06.961
Is that honestly what you think?

172
00:22:12.680 --> 00:22:17.919
I'll tell you who is to blame.
That prime minister from Holland.

173
00:22:17.998 --> 00:22:20.319
And his republican friends.

174
00:22:21.039 --> 00:22:25.477
They should send him out to sea.
- This isn't your fault.

175
00:22:25.597 --> 00:22:29.396
The Spanish want our trade routes.
the Germans want to control our rivers.

176
00:22:29.556 --> 00:22:34.275
And the French can't wait to occupy
the Southern Netherlands.

177
00:22:35.874 --> 00:22:37.754
What are we going to do?

178
00:22:59.949 --> 00:23:01.188
Just go.

179
00:23:05.949 --> 00:23:08.267
I made you a promise.

180
00:23:08.386 --> 00:23:11.947
There is no use staying home
if there is no home left.

181
00:23:14.986 --> 00:23:16.946
Engel. come on.

182
00:23:19.824 --> 00:23:24.384
We need a strong leader
who is respected by other kingdoms.

183
00:23:24.623 --> 00:23:27.544
What do we do about it?
- The Prince of Orange...

184
00:23:27.663 --> 00:23:29.582
is nothing but a brat.

185
00:23:30.342 --> 00:23:34.781
A brat. Are we sure
that the Prince is a real man?

186
00:23:36.261 --> 00:23:40.459
I've been told he prefers ballet
over military strategy.

187
00:23:44.618 --> 00:23:48.697
Order. order.
- Gentlemen.

188
00:23:48.818 --> 00:23:55.097
Let's keep it somewhat civilised.
What do you propose. regent Kievit?

189
00:23:56.937 --> 00:24:02.095
I propose we appoint
the honourable lord Cornelis Tromp...

190
00:24:02.216 --> 00:24:07.894
son of our greatest naval hero ever.
as our new admiral.

191
00:24:26.010 --> 00:24:29.049
Mr de Witt?
- Mr Tromp.

192
00:24:29.168 --> 00:24:31.609
Do we have an appointment?
- No. we don't.

193
00:24:31.808 --> 00:24:34.207
I thought I'd speed things up.

194
00:24:41.006 --> 00:24:43.965
Since your father's funeral
I haven't had a chance...

195
00:24:44.086 --> 00:24:46.925
You're looking for someone
to replace my father.

196
00:24:47.125 --> 00:24:50.644
I'm looking into it.
- You probably don't realize...

197
00:24:50.763 --> 00:24:54.323
but the fleet will only accept
one man as their new admiral.

198
00:24:54.483 --> 00:24:55.964
And who is that?

199
00:24:57.443 --> 00:25:01.322
My blood is his blood.
The blood of Bestevaer.

200
00:25:02.041 --> 00:25:03.920
You might not understand.

201
00:25:04.002 --> 00:25:07.920
I understand the admiral
was a father figure to his men.

202
00:25:07.999 --> 00:25:11.358
But Bestevaer is a title of respect.

203
00:25:11.520 --> 00:25:14.359
You have to earn it.
it's not hereditary.

204
00:25:15.279 --> 00:25:17.357
I'm afraid it is. Mr de Witt.

205
00:25:17.518 --> 00:25:21.518
Heroes father heroes.
that's how sailors see it.

206
00:25:21.716 --> 00:25:25.036
And that. Mr de Witt.
will never change.

207
00:25:29.115 --> 00:25:31.875
You're still thinking about De Ruyter?

208
00:25:31.954 --> 00:25:34.594
Why not invite him to dinner?

209
00:25:34.674 --> 00:25:38.513
Johan. he's stubborn.
-Invite his wife too. this time.

210
00:25:58.508 --> 00:26:02.428
Mr. and Mrs. De Ruyter. welcome. Come in.

211
00:26:09.545 --> 00:26:12.265
Was it a long trip. De Ruyter?

212
00:26:13.825 --> 00:26:15.824
From Vlissingen to The Hague.

213
00:26:15.905 --> 00:26:19.903
Of course.
- Darling. don't just stand there.

214
00:26:19.984 --> 00:26:23.502
Won't you offer our guests a drink?
- Yes.

215
00:26:23.622 --> 00:26:27.143
You didn't tell me they have a baby.
- My wife. Wendela.

216
00:26:27.262 --> 00:26:29.342
What a cutie.

217
00:26:29.461 --> 00:26:31.701
Excuse me.
- What for?

218
00:26:31.861 --> 00:26:35.301
She is a cutie.
I'll show you round the house.

219
00:26:35.459 --> 00:26:38.899
Wine?
Or do sailors only drink beer?

220
00:26:38.938 --> 00:26:43.138
Girls.
Why don't you show us around?

221
00:26:50.096 --> 00:26:53.855
We need larger ships with more cannons.

222
00:26:53.935 --> 00:26:55.775
Larger ships. fine.

223
00:26:57.054 --> 00:26:59.454
They must be agile
and have a shallow draught.

224
00:26:59.615 --> 00:27:01.854
Merchant ships are of no use to me.

225
00:27:01.934 --> 00:27:06.293
I'll arrange it. What else?
- Better pay for the crew.

226
00:27:08.532 --> 00:27:09.973
Higher wages?

227
00:27:10.131 --> 00:27:13.092
If they die.
they leave a family behind.

228
00:27:14.691 --> 00:27:16.171
Consider it done.

229
00:27:16.291 --> 00:27:18.930
Doesn't the parliament
have to approve. first?

230
00:27:19.051 --> 00:27:20.850
Leave that to me.

231
00:27:22.130 --> 00:27:25.969
Each winter. the fleet lies at anchor.
It's a waste of time.

232
00:27:26.048 --> 00:27:27.047
I agree.

233
00:27:27.168 --> 00:27:30.807
If I were admiral.
I'd train the crew in winter.

234
00:27:30.888 --> 00:27:34.126
Exactly.
And that costs money. too.

235
00:27:34.246 --> 00:27:37.406
Carry on. What else?
- The sea-battles?

236
00:27:37.526 --> 00:27:41.645
In battle now. it's every ship for itself.
It's total chaos.

237
00:27:41.845 --> 00:27:47.084
Organisation is key.
- You mentioned sign flags in the past.

238
00:27:47.164 --> 00:27:49.563
The English have been using them
for years.

239
00:27:49.684 --> 00:27:52.562
But their system is too limited.

240
00:27:53.842 --> 00:27:56.882
The ladies are chatting.
Mr prime minister?

241
00:27:57.001 --> 00:27:59.882
Allow me to introduce my brother.
Cornelis.

242
00:28:00.040 --> 00:28:02.316
Tell us about the
system we developed.

243
00:28:02.374 --> 00:28:05.058
Our system?
I happen to have it right here.

244
00:28:09.158 --> 00:28:11.438
We disagreed about the colours.

245
00:28:11.598 --> 00:28:14.917
Johan felt we were using too much orange.
- A bit too much.

246
00:28:15.877 --> 00:28:19.997
So. what do you say. De Ruyter?
Are you going to do this job?

247
00:28:20.196 --> 00:28:22.156
Or do you have more demands?

248
00:28:26.114 --> 00:28:30.433
I. Michiel Adriaenszoon de Ruyter...

249
00:28:30.554 --> 00:28:33.553
The English have
a limited flag system.

250
00:28:33.714 --> 00:28:37.193
We're expanding our flag system
with all these codes.

251
00:28:37.312 --> 00:28:44.551
...swear allegiance to the Republic
of the United Netherlands.

252
00:28:44.671 --> 00:28:49.509
And then change the signal. Only
these 6 bow cannons are a problem.

253
00:28:49.590 --> 00:28:52.669
We tack as fast as we can
and then...

254
00:29:13.223 --> 00:29:18.423
We fire everything we have
on the port side on these ships here.

255
00:29:18.542 --> 00:29:19.782
Fire.

256
00:29:20.863 --> 00:29:25.262
Cool and reload. Come on. Faster.

257
00:29:29.180 --> 00:29:32.020
And?
- We're here.

258
00:29:33.380 --> 00:29:34.900
Wait.

259
00:29:36.579 --> 00:29:42.217
Do you really think I look all right?
- You're the Prince of Orange.

260
00:29:42.297 --> 00:29:44.537
All of the Netherlands loves you.

261
00:29:53.616 --> 00:29:56.855
Huzzah. huzzah. huzzah.

262
00:30:01.213 --> 00:30:04.372
Your Highness.
- Prime minister.

263
00:30:04.452 --> 00:30:08.171
May I introduce gentlemen De Witt.
Tromp and our new admiral?

264
00:30:08.292 --> 00:30:11.171
Admiral De Ruyter. our great sea hero.

265
00:30:11.290 --> 00:30:14.650
You can't imagine
how glad I am to meet you.

266
00:30:14.769 --> 00:30:18.848
I want to hear all about your travels
to Africa and your escape from France.

267
00:30:18.930 --> 00:30:21.769
This is my wife. Anna.
- Your Highness.

268
00:30:21.848 --> 00:30:23.288
Fascinating.

269
00:30:24.528 --> 00:30:26.247
Fascinating.

270
00:30:30.887 --> 00:30:37.244
I promise to do my utmost
to truly follow...

271
00:30:37.485 --> 00:30:40.124
the instructions and orders...

272
00:30:40.364 --> 00:30:46.682
in regards to my position as admiral
- the Supreme Commander of the Fleet.

273
00:31:16.036 --> 00:31:19.555
You're very brave to be here Your Highness.
surrounded by these republicans.

274
00:31:20.515 --> 00:31:23.834
The English fleet has set sail.
- Four squadrons.

275
00:31:23.915 --> 00:31:26.673
They're blocking our merchant ships.

276
00:31:26.794 --> 00:31:29.992
We have to take action
before our goods are lost.

277
00:31:50.508 --> 00:31:54.106
One. two. all together...

278
00:31:54.268 --> 00:31:56.707
One. two. all together...

279
00:32:03.585 --> 00:32:08.503
One. two. all together...

280
00:32:09.664 --> 00:32:11.743
Work those ropes.

281
00:32:11.824 --> 00:32:14.022
Get that wind in the sails.

282
00:32:19.942 --> 00:32:22.580
Render those ropes further.

283
00:32:24.261 --> 00:32:25.940
Come on.

284
00:32:29.459 --> 00:32:31.779
One. two. all together...

285
00:32:50.775 --> 00:32:54.494
If the wind turns. the rear squadron
sails around them.

286
00:32:54.614 --> 00:32:59.012
So I have to keep an eye on your flags
while I'm surrounded by flying canon balls?

287
00:32:59.092 --> 00:33:01.891
Just give me an extra 150 men.
- No. it'll be chaos.

288
00:33:01.972 --> 00:33:04.812
The English have more ships.
bigger guns.

289
00:33:04.852 --> 00:33:08.770
We stick to the plan. Or do we want
another defeat like Lowestoft?

290
00:33:10.491 --> 00:33:14.008
We must make sure
we're well-organised.

291
00:33:14.128 --> 00:33:18.207
Good. we'll do it your way.
You stubborn Zeelander.

292
00:33:19.249 --> 00:33:22.166
Are you prepared to die
for the fatherland?

293
00:33:27.845 --> 00:33:30.684
To the fatherland.

294
00:33:41.963 --> 00:33:43.802
Wonderful.

295
00:33:43.923 --> 00:33:47.521
God bless you.
- Half a turn to port.

296
00:33:47.642 --> 00:33:50.600
Half a turn to port.

297
00:33:57.360 --> 00:34:00.318
What's going on?
- Gout.

298
00:34:00.439 --> 00:34:02.198
Am I in the way?
- Not at all.

299
00:34:02.358 --> 00:34:04.198
A perfect target for the English.

300
00:34:09.837 --> 00:34:13.556
The Royal Charles.
Unsinkable. or so they say.

301
00:34:13.675 --> 00:34:15.756
All ships are unsinkable. Jan.

302
00:34:17.915 --> 00:34:19.595
Until they sink.

303
00:34:59.865 --> 00:35:02.944
Signal: In line.
- You mean this one. sir?

304
00:35:03.063 --> 00:35:04.504
Put it up.

305
00:35:27.858 --> 00:35:28.823
It's impressive.

306
00:35:28.881 --> 00:35:31.716
You'll see.
it'll be every ship for itself.

307
00:35:43.974 --> 00:35:45.815
Captain.
- Yes. sir.

308
00:35:45.934 --> 00:35:51.094
Vanguard closer to the wind.
- Vanguard. luff up.

309
00:35:53.933 --> 00:35:55.652
Ready to go about. now.

310
00:35:56.732 --> 00:36:01.530
Pull up the mizzen sail.

311
00:36:01.651 --> 00:36:05.730
Come on. keep pulling those braces.

312
00:36:48.080 --> 00:36:52.359
Load starboard.
- Load starboard.

313
00:36:52.478 --> 00:36:55.278
Do you want me to call your mother?

314
00:36:55.399 --> 00:36:59.718
Get to work. Faster.
- Faster.

315
00:37:11.675 --> 00:37:13.875
Mainsail halyard.

316
00:37:22.952 --> 00:37:26.392
Come on. load. Faster.

317
00:37:37.508 --> 00:37:39.948
Faster.
- Keep it in the wind.

318
00:38:17.059 --> 00:38:18.780
Brace yourselves.

319
00:38:19.859 --> 00:38:22.019
Wait.
- Wait.

320
00:38:23.378 --> 00:38:24.938
Wait.

321
00:38:25.978 --> 00:38:29.458
Everybody wait.

322
00:38:29.738 --> 00:38:33.136
Jibs forward.
- Luff up.

323
00:38:36.775 --> 00:38:39.054
Wait.

324
00:38:52.892 --> 00:38:54.452
Attention.

325
00:39:20.245 --> 00:39:21.245
Admiral?

326
00:39:24.964 --> 00:39:29.404
Trim the lines.

327
00:39:33.163 --> 00:39:34.522
Fire.

328
00:40:07.475 --> 00:40:10.274
Let him be.
Get back. Keep firing.

329
00:40:21.791 --> 00:40:26.591
Pull up the mizzen sail. Luff up.

330
00:40:26.671 --> 00:40:30.910
Come on. get going.
- Come on.

331
00:40:31.030 --> 00:40:33.388
They need to reload faster. Come on.

332
00:41:02.102 --> 00:41:05.422
You're too slow.
- Why is it taking so long?

333
00:41:05.501 --> 00:41:08.501
Faster. or you're going overboard.

334
00:41:12.699 --> 00:41:14.899
Speed it up. Come on. boy.

335
00:41:15.060 --> 00:41:17.018
I need to shit.
- No shitting.

336
00:41:17.138 --> 00:41:21.218
Reload the cannon.
You can have that shit later.

337
00:41:22.697 --> 00:41:26.696
Come on. Reload the cannons.
Reload like lightning.

338
00:41:26.816 --> 00:41:29.376
Come on. reload.

339
00:41:31.095 --> 00:41:37.374
Get back to work. Get back to that
cannon. Are you sleeping or what?

340
00:41:39.094 --> 00:41:41.813
Captain. how is the rear?

341
00:41:41.934 --> 00:41:45.692
The English are on lee side.
- Middle squadron luff up.

342
00:41:45.811 --> 00:41:48.092
Gijs. middle squadron luff up.

343
00:41:59.929 --> 00:42:03.808
Hold the lines.
- Get that wind in the sails.

344
00:42:03.927 --> 00:42:07.087
Port. Keep going.

345
00:42:19.244 --> 00:42:23.804
Reload the cannons. starboard. port.

346
00:42:24.883 --> 00:42:27.403
Look. that Englishman is mine.

347
00:42:27.483 --> 00:42:30.682
Two points port.
- We need to stay in line.

348
00:42:30.801 --> 00:42:34.241
Two points port.
- But the signal from De Ruyter.

349
00:42:42.439 --> 00:42:44.320
All right. come about.

350
00:42:44.440 --> 00:42:49.678
Come about. Brace the sails.

351
00:42:59.835 --> 00:43:03.475
Load port cannons.

352
00:43:05.075 --> 00:43:06.594
Cover.

353
00:43:08.233 --> 00:43:10.192
Fire.

354
00:43:26.229 --> 00:43:28.028
Keep that head in the wind.

355
00:43:28.668 --> 00:43:31.746
De Ruyter's strategy is not going to work.

356
00:43:34.027 --> 00:43:36.346
And we're the ones under fire.

357
00:43:39.585 --> 00:43:42.304
Load port cannons.

358
00:43:45.304 --> 00:43:47.583
What are you doing? Get in position.

359
00:43:47.703 --> 00:43:49.463
Load port cannons.

360
00:44:08.258 --> 00:44:10.618
Grappling hooks.

361
00:44:10.737 --> 00:44:14.777
A portion of rum for the man who puts
the most English to the sword.

362
00:45:07.445 --> 00:45:08.604

363
00:45:53.594 --> 00:45:56.154
Do you want a hug from De Witt?

364
00:46:30.307 --> 00:46:36.024
Victory is ours. A cheer for Tromp.

365
00:46:37.664 --> 00:46:41.424
A cheer for Piet's cannons.

366
00:46:41.504 --> 00:46:44.223
A cheer for our captain.

367
00:46:45.223 --> 00:46:50.141
And three cheers for our admiral.

368
00:47:32.572 --> 00:47:35.812
Can His Highness receive me?
- Certainly.

369
00:47:54.206 --> 00:47:56.726
Your Highness. lord Kievit.

370
00:47:58.525 --> 00:48:01.525
Our fleet has given
the English a beating.

371
00:48:01.685 --> 00:48:04.965
So De Ruyter is as good as they say.

372
00:48:05.044 --> 00:48:08.803
Quite a victory for Johan de Witt.
- For the Netherlands.

373
00:48:08.883 --> 00:48:10.804
Gentlemen?
- Of course.

374
00:48:11.882 --> 00:48:14.043
While I stand by doing nothing.

375
00:48:14.202 --> 00:48:17.921
All my relatives and friends
are kings or important people.

376
00:48:18.082 --> 00:48:23.119
Even those Habsburger simpletons.
with their in-bred minds.

377
00:48:24.240 --> 00:48:28.119
Why doesn't anyone take
the Prince of Orange seriously?

378
00:48:28.239 --> 00:48:31.877
You can play a decisive role.
If I may be so bold.

379
00:48:34.958 --> 00:48:38.277
You're the cousin of the English king.

380
00:49:29.546 --> 00:49:35.464
So. 7200. 8400. 10.800
amounts to a total of 5.14 percent.

381
00:49:35.584 --> 00:49:39.422
As I was saying. we can calculate
average life expectancy.

382
00:49:39.583 --> 00:49:41.941
And adapt the price of annuities.

383
00:49:42.023 --> 00:49:45.142
If my calculations are correct...
- They are.

384
00:49:46.182 --> 00:49:48.301
Indeed they are.

385
00:49:48.420 --> 00:49:52.899
The 7.14 percent the State
is paying out now. is far too high.

386
00:49:53.061 --> 00:49:55.378
So. we can save a lot of money.

387
00:49:55.460 --> 00:49:58.858
Money the State can use
to build more ships.

388
00:50:04.057 --> 00:50:09.497
But. must people die earlier or later
to make this work?

389
00:50:09.617 --> 00:50:11.935
Exactly. it's not clear.

390
00:50:13.296 --> 00:50:15.374
It's not clear.

391
00:50:15.495 --> 00:50:19.653
I'll explain one more time
what the percentages mean.

392
00:50:21.134 --> 00:50:24.573
Why earlier?
- Gentlemen. please excuse us.

393
00:50:27.052 --> 00:50:29.971
Didn't you say
you could explain it to a child?

394
00:50:33.210 --> 00:50:36.410
The English have sailed again. sir.

395
00:50:37.449 --> 00:50:41.449
De Ruyter will have to get ready.
- Sounds like a good idea.

396
00:51:02.285 --> 00:51:03.564
Thanks. guys.

397
00:51:20.161 --> 00:51:23.000
That goes in the kitchen.
and that one.

398
00:51:23.119 --> 00:51:25.358
And that one goes to the study.

399
00:51:25.479 --> 00:51:28.438
Are you sure?
- Yes.

400
00:51:28.517 --> 00:51:31.637
Need a hand?
- Michiel.

401
00:51:31.798 --> 00:51:35.036
Aren't you sailing tomorrow?
- Yes. with the first tide.

402
00:51:35.157 --> 00:51:38.316
I thought we'd have dinner together.
- Daddy.

403
00:51:40.954 --> 00:51:43.355
I have my own room.
- You live here too?

404
00:51:43.474 --> 00:51:46.953
We have our own box bed.
- Go ahead. I'll be right in.

405
00:51:47.114 --> 00:51:51.114
The admiralty suggested a larger house.
but this is near the harbour.

406
00:51:51.233 --> 00:51:53.431
As long as you live here.

407
00:51:55.552 --> 00:51:57.272
Dad. are you coming?

408
00:52:07.509 --> 00:52:11.228
Dad. this is our bed.
- Look at that.

409
00:52:12.228 --> 00:52:14.868
No boots in bed.

410
00:52:15.907 --> 00:52:18.106
You sound just like your mother.

411
00:52:19.746 --> 00:52:22.105
What are you doing?

412
00:52:31.623 --> 00:52:35.342
VOC? Can I have a look?
- Go ahead.

413
00:52:42.740 --> 00:52:47.981
Flooded cellar?
- I'll take the supplier off my list.

414
00:52:48.100 --> 00:52:50.779
Don't bother.
- What?

415
00:52:52.019 --> 00:52:55.818
You can't do this.
I've supplied the fleet for years.

416
00:52:55.898 --> 00:52:58.338
Why do we get the worst grain?

417
00:52:59.377 --> 00:53:01.977
Or do you supply this muck
to the VOC too?

418
00:53:04.897 --> 00:53:06.376
Is there a problem?

419
00:53:09.135 --> 00:53:12.774
You don't get better grain
for your republican pals.

420
00:53:15.573 --> 00:53:18.972
Who does he think he is?
We'll find someone else.

421
00:53:21.012 --> 00:53:23.332
What?
- That was the third one.

422
00:53:25.251 --> 00:53:26.890
Why didn't you tell me?

423
00:53:27.091 --> 00:53:30.009
Because you're busy
saving the country.

424
00:55:32.023 --> 00:55:34.022
Come and join me.

425
00:57:18.718 --> 00:57:20.038
Are you all right?

426
00:57:20.998 --> 00:57:22.437
Leave me. I want to be alone.

427
00:57:29.756 --> 00:57:33.275
Faster. guys.
- Come about.

428
00:57:34.234 --> 00:57:37.874
Keep it tight.

429
00:57:42.553 --> 00:57:44.472
What are they doing?
- Gijs.

430
00:57:44.872 --> 00:57:49.231
They try to cut us off.
Take the signals to the front now.

431
00:57:49.351 --> 00:57:53.110
Tack over port.
- Ready to come about.

432
00:57:53.191 --> 00:57:55.269
Full about now.

433
00:58:22.143 --> 00:58:24.663
Get to work on the lower decks.

434
00:58:25.983 --> 00:58:28.463
Keep it UP-

435
00:58:32.581 --> 00:58:36.700
Follow those two ships there.
- We'll break the line. Tromp.

436
00:58:36.820 --> 00:58:40.380
Sod off with your line.
those ships are mine.

437
00:58:40.499 --> 00:58:44.018
Four points to starboard.
- Michiel ordered it.

438
00:58:44.938 --> 00:58:48.098
Who is the highest ranking officer?
Come about.

439
00:58:49.138 --> 00:58:52.897
Four points to starboard.
Come about.

440
00:59:28.248 --> 00:59:31.848
Where is Tromp?
- He has broken line.

441
00:59:34.527 --> 00:59:36.686
Cannons ready?

442
00:59:50.763 --> 00:59:51.964
Fire.

443
01:00:07.959 --> 01:00:09.479
Damn it.

444
01:00:11.199 --> 01:00:12.839
God damn it.

445
01:01:03.905 --> 01:01:07.665
Michiel. they're surrounding us.
- Where is Tromp?

446
01:01:17.023 --> 01:01:18.582
Keep pulling.

447
01:01:49.455 --> 01:01:52.855
I'm sorry. admiral.
- Lie still. don't move.

448
01:01:53.654 --> 01:01:55.414
Admiral?

449
01:01:57.534 --> 01:01:59.294
It doesn't hurt at all.

450
01:02:31.926 --> 01:02:36.885
You're the rock on which I build. the
future awaiting me. my highest good.

451
01:02:37.004 --> 01:02:41.123
Seventeen killed on the gunners' deck.
All of them brought up.

452
01:02:42.323 --> 01:02:47.163
You're the rock on which I build. the
future awaiting me. my highest good.

453
01:02:47.242 --> 01:02:48.281
Hang in there.

454
01:03:15.155 --> 01:03:17.076
I've lost twenty ships.

455
01:03:17.155 --> 01:03:20.353
Who was in command?
- I gave you an order.

456
01:03:20.515 --> 01:03:24.074
So court-martial me.
- Get back into that longboat.

457
01:03:24.193 --> 01:03:29.273
Don't set foot on my ship or on any
other ship in this fleet. ever again.

458
01:03:29.352 --> 01:03:32.832
You are relieved of your duties
as of now. so piss off.

459
01:03:32.991 --> 01:03:37.191
Leave it to the court-martial.
- You disgrace the name of Tromp.

460
01:03:39.910 --> 01:03:42.110
Leave my father out of this.

461
01:03:44.269 --> 01:03:46.829
He'd be ashamed of you.

462
01:03:55.587 --> 01:03:57.466
Michiel. you can't do this.

463
01:03:57.585 --> 01:04:00.905
You want to be dishonourably
discharged as well?

464
01:04:04.065 --> 01:04:05.664
Come on. back to work.

465
01:04:05.824 --> 01:04:09.063
Get down there
and pick up those cannons.

466
01:04:46.815 --> 01:04:52.893
Master Buat is a loyal rittmeister.
You're executing such a loyal servant?

467
01:04:53.014 --> 01:04:57.212
Who is he serving? He went to
the king of England behind my back.

468
01:04:57.291 --> 01:05:00.451
In the national interest.
- Your interest.

469
01:05:03.611 --> 01:05:05.329
I've seen enough.

470
01:05:37.483 --> 01:05:41.763
I shouldn't have lost my temper
with Tromp.

471
01:05:43.282 --> 01:05:47.240
He is the vice-admiral. after all.
- He deserved it.

472
01:05:50.640 --> 01:05:53.319
Stay down or I'll put this
you know where.

473
01:05:55.599 --> 01:05:59.238
It's just a cold.
- Malaria.

474
01:06:04.037 --> 01:06:06.076
Where is the patient?
- Upstairs.

475
01:06:06.157 --> 01:06:08.555
De Ruyter?
- That's Johan.

476
01:06:10.876 --> 01:06:12.795
Do what you have to do.

477
01:06:15.314 --> 01:06:19.314
We haven't heard anything from the English.
- They've run out of money.

478
01:06:20.793 --> 01:06:24.151
So why won't they negotiate peace?

479
01:06:25.111 --> 01:06:29.151
They hope we're afraid of the French.
We can't afford two wars.

480
01:06:29.232 --> 01:06:33.430
The French? Are they a real threat?
- No. but the Orangists are.

481
01:06:33.550 --> 01:06:36.430
They say I'm too weak
to force a peace treaty.

482
01:06:38.669 --> 01:06:41.547
You must force the English
to their knees.

483
01:06:44.268 --> 01:06:46.027
You have a plan.

484
01:06:48.387 --> 01:06:50.507
It's not without risk.

485
01:06:50.746 --> 01:06:53.666
You know the English fleet
is in Chatham.

486
01:06:53.825 --> 01:06:56.825
With the right wind
it's only a two day sail inland.

487
01:06:56.944 --> 01:07:00.504
You want to sail up the Medway?
- Yes. What?

488
01:07:00.623 --> 01:07:03.064
Is it crazy?
Would nobody do it?

489
01:07:03.263 --> 01:07:06.103
Sail through their chains?

490
01:07:06.222 --> 01:07:10.262
You must be desperate.
- I know it's a lot to ask for.

491
01:07:10.341 --> 01:07:14.180
Not now. get out of here.
- Sorry. dad.

492
01:07:19.779 --> 01:07:22.979
What about those sea soldiers
you're training?

493
01:07:23.098 --> 01:07:26.618
What do you call them?
- Marines.

494
01:07:27.459 --> 01:07:29.578
Is this a good time to test them?

495
01:07:31.058 --> 01:07:32.417
It's a bad time.

496
01:07:33.657 --> 01:07:36.255
Not even men like that
can be asked to...

497
01:07:45.094 --> 01:07:49.013
Forget about it. it's a silly plan.
Really silly.

498
01:08:11.927 --> 01:08:14.646
Which one do you want?
That one?

499
01:08:17.806 --> 01:08:19.646
Thank you.
- Bye.

500
01:08:23.205 --> 01:08:24.806
Hi. darling.
- Dad's up.

501
01:08:27.524 --> 01:08:29.005
What are you doing?

502
01:08:30.204 --> 01:08:32.043
Try to understand.

503
01:08:32.162 --> 01:08:34.923
If I don't go...
- Where are you going?

504
01:08:35.962 --> 01:08:37.722
Can't you tell me?

505
01:08:39.562 --> 01:08:41.241
That's a first.

506
01:09:00.596 --> 01:09:04.196
The Lord bless you and keep you.

507
01:09:04.315 --> 01:09:08.356
The Lord make his face shine on you
and be gracious to you.

508
01:09:08.434 --> 01:09:11.913
The Lord turn his face toward you...

509
01:09:12.034 --> 01:09:15.434
and give you peace.
- Amen.

510
01:09:21.591 --> 01:09:25.152
Thank you. my thoughts
are with admiral De Ruyter.

511
01:09:25.271 --> 01:09:26.630
Thank you.

512
01:09:31.990 --> 01:09:33.189
For my husband.

513
01:09:33.310 --> 01:09:37.228
I don't know...
- You know where they are.

514
01:09:37.349 --> 01:09:40.708
For my husband.
- For my son.

515
01:10:43.172 --> 01:10:45.213
Where is Michiel?

516
01:10:45.332 --> 01:10:48.612
These women have no idea
where their husbands are.

517
01:10:48.812 --> 01:10:50.812
Johan must know.

518
01:10:52.810 --> 01:10:55.889
Johan. I'm sorry to disturb you.

519
01:10:56.609 --> 01:10:59.968
Anna is here. Where is the fleet?
Where is Michiel?

520
01:11:00.609 --> 01:11:03.408
I don't know. I can't reach them.

521
01:11:04.489 --> 01:11:06.448
Tell her that yourself.

522
01:11:11.007 --> 01:11:12.526
Come on in.

523
01:11:25.804 --> 01:11:28.843
They're on the Medway.
- Heading for London?

524
01:11:58.356 --> 01:11:59.876
It's time.

525
01:12:00.875 --> 01:12:04.875
Gentlemen. the people
are counting on you.

526
01:12:07.193 --> 01:12:08.594
Over to you.

527
01:12:10.512 --> 01:12:13.313
Men. into the longboats.

528
01:12:40.387 --> 01:12:41.825
Down.

529
01:12:44.025 --> 01:12:45.025
Up.

530
01:12:47.225 --> 01:12:48.744
Forward.

531
01:13:32.454 --> 01:13:34.973
Those brothers De Witt.

532
01:14:36.240 --> 01:14:37.640
Watch out.

533
01:14:50.636 --> 01:14:51.796

534
01:15:02.874 --> 01:15:06.112
It's a shame to burn that one.

535
01:15:09.591 --> 01:15:12.272
Members of the State.
I present to you...

536
01:15:12.391 --> 01:15:15.111
the stern carving
of the Royal Charles.

537
01:15:26.309 --> 01:15:28.907
You didn't expect that one. eh?

538
01:15:47.982 --> 01:15:53.062
Charles ll has accepted our terms.
The peace treaty will be signed in Breda.

539
01:15:54.742 --> 01:15:57.301
Van Ginneken. let me embrace you.

540
01:16:45.529 --> 01:16:47.210
I can't do it.

541
01:16:47.770 --> 01:16:50.488
Delicious. It looks fantastic.

542
01:16:50.689 --> 01:16:52.048
Well.

543
01:16:53.008 --> 01:16:54.847
I propose a toast.
- Again?

544
01:16:54.927 --> 01:16:57.807
To peace.
- We've already toasted to that.

545
01:16:57.887 --> 01:17:01.567
To us.
- That's much better. To us.

546
01:17:01.686 --> 01:17:07.165
Can we go and play now?
- Yes. go and play. Quickly now.

547
01:17:07.285 --> 01:17:08.644
Be careful.

548
01:17:08.964 --> 01:17:10.524
Not too fast.

549
01:17:15.724 --> 01:17:18.962
What? Should I have proposed
a toast to the Prince?

550
01:17:19.083 --> 01:17:22.762
This peace won't last.
-It's politics. One day at a time.

551
01:17:22.882 --> 01:17:26.561
Michiel is worried about the French.
- You mean you are.

552
01:17:26.680 --> 01:17:30.920
So. everything is fine?
The French are building up their troops.

553
01:17:31.039 --> 01:17:33.480
Rumours.
- Persistent rumours.

554
01:17:33.638 --> 01:17:37.117
So you want to expand the army?
- We should have done that already.

555
01:17:37.158 --> 01:17:41.796
The army is full of Orangists. How many
batallions will you give the Prince?

556
01:17:41.917 --> 01:17:45.116
You're asking for a civil war.
- Cornelis means...

557
01:17:45.317 --> 01:17:49.234
I think I know what he means.
Damn it.

558
01:17:50.996 --> 01:17:52.475
Idiot.

559
01:17:54.834 --> 01:17:57.554
Can't we just enjoy ourselves
for once?

560
01:17:57.713 --> 01:18:02.473
We're at peace with the English. The
republicans hold a stable majority.

561
01:18:02.671 --> 01:18:06.031
In the meeting hall.
- Useless when the French invade.

562
01:18:06.111 --> 01:18:09.111
They never will.
- The people are scared.

563
01:18:09.190 --> 01:18:12.790
That's silly of them.
-It's all my men talk about. too.

564
01:18:12.909 --> 01:18:16.789
Diplomacy. Michiel.
diplomacy is the future of warfare.

565
01:18:16.910 --> 01:18:19.548
The people don't understand diplomacy.

566
01:18:22.868 --> 01:18:27.106
I can't adapt my policy to people
who understand less than we do.

567
01:18:31.866 --> 01:18:35.104
Come on. gentlemen.
we're having a party.

568
01:18:36.664 --> 01:18:39.503
I'm going to dance
with my fantastic wife.

569
01:18:46.422 --> 01:18:49.302
You heard the man.
we're having a party.

570
01:18:54.021 --> 01:18:55.940
Mr Chairman...

571
01:18:56.980 --> 01:19:00.940
they say that Louis
is gathering 100.000 troops.

572
01:19:01.059 --> 01:19:04.498
They say. they say...
Who says so? Who?

573
01:19:04.659 --> 01:19:09.698
Mr Van Ginneken has it easy with
his district behind the defence lines.

574
01:19:09.856 --> 01:19:11.736
Order.

575
01:19:14.336 --> 01:19:15.815
Mr Chairman...

576
01:19:15.936 --> 01:19:20.094
we've been paying huge taxes.

577
01:19:20.214 --> 01:19:22.973
And what are we getting in return?

578
01:19:23.094 --> 01:19:26.772
Give up the south and perhaps
Louis will levy less taxes.

579
01:19:26.893 --> 01:19:30.452
Would you say that to my face?
- I certainly would.

580
01:19:30.612 --> 01:19:33.851
I'll repeat it to your face:
Give up the south.

581
01:19:35.091 --> 01:19:37.690
Order. order.

582
01:19:38.371 --> 01:19:40.089
Gentlemen.

583
01:19:40.209 --> 01:19:44.329
Louis can mass all the troops
he wants. but he can't attack us.

584
01:19:45.089 --> 01:19:49.968
He'll face the Swedes and the English.
We have it in black and white.

585
01:19:50.368 --> 01:19:55.166
What if Charles breaks his word?
- We are on good terms with England.

586
01:19:57.686 --> 01:20:00.484
Right honourable member Kievit...

587
01:20:01.166 --> 01:20:04.564
I hope you're not suffering
from sleepless nights?

588
01:20:06.684 --> 01:20:09.883
I'd sleep better
if the Prince were king.

589
01:20:10.004 --> 01:20:13.882
Only then we know for sure
that Charles won't betray us.

590
01:20:26.920 --> 01:20:31.918
You're responsible for the civil war
in this country. You. Mr De Witt.

591
01:20:32.037 --> 01:20:33.637
Damn you.

592
01:21:57.059 --> 01:22:00.578
The French are in Maastricht
with 100.000 soldiers.

593
01:22:00.697 --> 01:22:03.937
And Louis XIV is there himself.
- Not bad for us.

594
01:22:04.776 --> 01:22:08.576
Not bad for us?
What do you mean?

595
01:22:08.657 --> 01:22:11.256
Do you realise
what is about to happen?

596
01:22:11.375 --> 01:22:14.494
Your Highness can save the country.

597
01:22:14.575 --> 01:22:18.174
And become supreme commander.
- And king.

598
01:22:18.294 --> 01:22:23.373
Charles has forged a deal with Louis.
- Charles has agreed not to interfere.

599
01:22:25.172 --> 01:22:26.852
Don't you get it?

600
01:22:28.052 --> 01:22:32.010
And you don't get it either?
You don't get it either.

601
01:22:33.170 --> 01:22:36.810
Do you think Charles
would give our country to Louis?

602
01:22:41.529 --> 01:22:43.689
The English will invade Holland.

603
01:22:57.725 --> 01:22:59.645
Go on. I'll finish this.

604
01:23:01.764 --> 01:23:03.523
Have you heard the news?

605
01:23:03.604 --> 01:23:07.363
The French are at the border.
- The English near the coast.

606
01:23:07.483 --> 01:23:08.683
And that's not all.

607
01:23:08.841 --> 01:23:12.442
The bishops of Cologne and Münster
are joining in.

608
01:23:12.561 --> 01:23:16.521
They've divided our country.
everyone gets a piece of the pie.

609
01:23:17.441 --> 01:23:19.280
It's not just about destroying our fleet.

610
01:23:19.439 --> 01:23:23.758
They want to land near The Hague
with a huge number of troops.

611
01:23:23.878 --> 01:23:27.678
You must stop them.
Our land army won't survive it.

612
01:23:27.798 --> 01:23:30.037
You're our only hope. Michiel.

613
01:23:30.198 --> 01:23:33.917
Don't let them turn us
into English and French provinces.

614
01:23:39.755 --> 01:23:43.595
Has it got worse again?
- I could do with some fresh air.

615
01:23:43.675 --> 01:23:46.514
It's better you stay with him.

616
01:23:48.274 --> 01:23:49.594
Thank you.

617
01:24:00.151 --> 01:24:02.630
I should never have weakened our army.

618
01:24:07.829 --> 01:24:10.028
If only I had fixed this earlier.

619
01:24:14.187 --> 01:24:17.187
This country has been blessed
to have you.

620
01:24:17.306 --> 01:24:19.587
No one could've predicted this.

621
01:24:23.185 --> 01:24:25.466
To the admiralty.

622
01:24:29.305 --> 01:24:31.863
Go on.
- Long live the prime minister.

623
01:24:31.983 --> 01:24:34.943
What was that?
You did not cheer for our Prince?

624
01:24:44.180 --> 01:24:48.139
Are you on Charles ll's pay roll?
Do you work for the English?

625
01:24:49.099 --> 01:24:53.579
I suggest you leave this sailor alone.
We'll be needing him.

626
01:24:53.699 --> 01:24:55.377
Get lost.

627
01:24:56.498 --> 01:24:59.696
Aren't you brave?
Losers.

628
01:25:00.777 --> 01:25:04.375
You're going back to Vlissingen.
- No. I'm staying here.

629
01:25:04.456 --> 01:25:07.254
You're so stubborn.
- Look who's talking.

630
01:25:07.336 --> 01:25:09.135
Engel. get inside.

631
01:25:12.455 --> 01:25:13.814
I can do this myself.

632
01:25:15.933 --> 01:25:19.573
I'll take care of him.
you take the girls to Vlissingen.

633
01:25:19.692 --> 01:25:21.572
Who says it's safer there?

634
01:25:21.651 --> 01:25:25.491
They think we're traitors
who work for the republicans.

635
01:26:34.755 --> 01:26:36.395
Eat your vegetables.

636
01:26:37.355 --> 01:26:41.395
I could hardly get through.
- Eat up before it gets cold.

637
01:26:42.354 --> 01:26:45.153
There are more and more of them.

638
01:26:45.234 --> 01:26:49.991
Why are those people so angry?
- Because they're afraid.

639
01:26:55.151 --> 01:26:57.071
First. they betrayed us...

640
01:26:58.311 --> 01:27:01.549
to the English and now to the French.

641
01:27:01.990 --> 01:27:04.189
And De Ruyter is part of it. too.

642
01:27:04.308 --> 01:27:07.548
If he wanted.
he could have chased them off.

643
01:27:09.548 --> 01:27:12.627
I've heard that he's keeping our ships
in the harbour.

644
01:27:12.746 --> 01:27:18.385
And that Louis wil make the admiral
the Duke of Brabant.

645
01:27:18.504 --> 01:27:21.544
The prime minister
has weakened the army...

646
01:27:21.665 --> 01:27:24.264
so De Ruyter has all the power.

647
01:27:25.224 --> 01:27:27.424
Downstairs. now.

648
01:27:30.062 --> 01:27:31.663
Hide.

649
01:27:42.859 --> 01:27:47.699
Mummy. hurry up. Come on.

650
01:27:47.738 --> 01:27:49.337
Stay there.

651
01:27:57.176 --> 01:27:58.897
Let's burn his house down.

652
01:28:05.495 --> 01:28:08.134
Fire.

653
01:28:08.294 --> 01:28:12.334
Go back. Go on. Just sit there.

654
01:28:18.332 --> 01:28:20.771
Here's a blanket. madam.

655
01:28:22.931 --> 01:28:26.090
Be careful.

656
01:28:42.406 --> 01:28:45.365
Don't you have anything better to do?

657
01:28:45.526 --> 01:28:49.924
Go back to your families.
- Your husband betrayed us.

658
01:28:50.044 --> 01:28:53.083
Betrayed you? Really?

659
01:28:54.524 --> 01:28:58.643
So what did my husband do when
the English attacked us at Plymouth?

660
01:28:59.641 --> 01:29:04.680
And Ter Heijde. and Bergen
and Chatham?

661
01:29:06.600 --> 01:29:09.120
Did he betray you then?

662
01:29:09.201 --> 01:29:12.920
Or did my husband save you
and your families?

663
01:29:14.519 --> 01:29:18.598
I understand that you're afraid.
I'm afraid. too.

664
01:29:20.798 --> 01:29:26.155
So go home and let Michiel do
what he always does.

665
01:29:26.275 --> 01:29:32.075
Risking his life so that all of you
can sleep safely.

666
01:29:34.194 --> 01:29:37.753
He tried to murder the Prince.
together with De Witt.

667
01:30:02.108 --> 01:30:03.068
Don't leave. mommy.

668
01:30:03.189 --> 01:30:05.428
It'll be all right.
- I'm afraid.

669
01:30:24.342 --> 01:30:26.383
Long live France.

670
01:30:38.820 --> 01:30:43.138
You don't have a plan. admit it.
- Mr De Waerd.

671
01:30:43.259 --> 01:30:48.218
Cut it out. Stop delaying things.

672
01:30:48.337 --> 01:30:52.577
There is no time for political games.
- It isn't a political game.

673
01:30:52.696 --> 01:30:55.096
If the Prince gets in charge...

674
01:31:32.328 --> 01:31:35.566
Representative De Waerd has the floor.

675
01:31:38.567 --> 01:31:41.445
The situation is untenable.

676
01:31:41.525 --> 01:31:45.844
The only person who can save us.
is the Prince.

677
01:31:46.005 --> 01:31:51.884
The prime minister should
hand in his resignation. Immediately.

678
01:32:24.796 --> 01:32:27.835
They're waiting. Your Highness.

679
01:32:27.915 --> 01:32:31.474
It took them such a long time.
Let them wait.

680
01:32:33.234 --> 01:32:38.312
I say we appoint Tromp as the new admiral.
- Someone we can trust.

681
01:32:38.433 --> 01:32:41.831
Since when can't I trust De Ruyter?

682
01:32:41.992 --> 01:32:44.630
But. Your Highness.
he's friends with De Witt.

683
01:32:44.751 --> 01:32:49.190
Please try to understand. Kievit.
we have to work together.

684
01:32:49.309 --> 01:32:51.669
I want to be the leader
for all Dutchmen.

685
01:33:05.747 --> 01:33:09.425
Your Highness. it's an honour
and pleasure to ask you...

686
01:33:09.506 --> 01:33:14.664
on behalf of the Dutch Republic
to accept the title of king...

687
01:33:14.785 --> 01:33:18.062
like your ancestor.
William of Orange. once was.

688
01:33:19.063 --> 01:33:24.743
There is one thing
I'm really concerned about.

689
01:33:25.461 --> 01:33:30.381
Yes. we have received
some very worrying news.

690
01:33:31.460 --> 01:33:35.300
Concerning a secret plot
to assassinate the Prince.

691
01:33:35.420 --> 01:33:37.179
We also know who's behind it.

692
01:33:56.694 --> 01:34:00.054
Come on.

693
01:34:00.133 --> 01:34:02.173
Go on.

694
01:34:03.093 --> 01:34:07.932
I can make this a lot easier for you.
All you have to do. is tell the truth.

695
01:34:08.092 --> 01:34:13.250
You were part of a conspiracy
to assassinate the Prince of Orange.

696
01:34:13.370 --> 01:34:14.971
There are witnesses.

697
01:34:19.289 --> 01:34:24.968
I don't see how you want to deny...
- Yes. that's highly unfortunate.

698
01:34:46.682 --> 01:34:49.921
I can't turn this into more
than an exile.

699
01:34:50.042 --> 01:34:52.920
I assume you don't want
to end up here yourself.

700
01:35:21.835 --> 01:35:23.714
I think you should read this.

701
01:35:26.672 --> 01:35:30.832
Cornelis is accused of high treason
for plotting to kill the Prince.

702
01:35:30.953 --> 01:35:33.832
Johan asks me to testify.
- Don't be stupid.

703
01:35:33.951 --> 01:35:36.951
You heard me.
- The brothers De Witt are lost.

704
01:35:37.110 --> 01:35:39.789
Stay out of it.
- What kind of country would that be?

705
01:35:39.909 --> 01:35:42.748
I say whatever I want.
as long as I live.

706
01:35:42.830 --> 01:35:46.229
Back to shore. straight away.
Hoist the sails.

707
01:36:01.464 --> 01:36:03.944
We have to get his brother
here as well.

708
01:36:05.864 --> 01:36:09.704
Say that this comes from Cornelis.
- I don't know if I...

709
01:36:11.863 --> 01:36:14.781
We're going to be in power soon.

710
01:36:14.983 --> 01:36:18.260
We need to know who is with us
and who is not.

711
01:36:30.379 --> 01:36:34.138
There must be some kind of procedure.
- That depends on...

712
01:36:34.298 --> 01:36:35.618
A message for you.

713
01:36:42.695 --> 01:36:46.374
Excuse me.
- Something must be done.

714
01:36:46.495 --> 01:36:47.735
Come on.

715
01:37:11.408 --> 01:37:15.569
Stand aside. Move. Open up.

716
01:37:29.245 --> 01:37:31.364
It's okay. It's me.

717
01:37:31.485 --> 01:37:36.924
You shouldn't have come. It's a trap.

718
01:37:38.322 --> 01:37:41.122
Admit it. You can't do without me.

719
01:37:51.080 --> 01:37:54.920
We have to get out of here.
Can you walk? I've got you.

720
01:38:16.194 --> 01:38:20.554
And you don't know where he went?
- No. sir. I don't. Good evening.

721
01:39:42.934 --> 01:39:43.893
Traitor.

722
01:40:19.165 --> 01:40:20.606
I want to have his dick.

723
01:41:13.513 --> 01:41:14.594
Do it.

724
01:41:32.669 --> 01:41:37.068
There is De Ruyter. He's friends
with the De Witts. Get him.

725
01:41:37.947 --> 01:41:39.628
Get him.

726
01:42:04.542 --> 01:42:07.620
The heart of the prime minister.

727
01:42:44.052 --> 01:42:46.291
I thought you were at sea.
- Daddy.

728
01:42:47.972 --> 01:42:51.050
Where have you been?
- The Hague.

729
01:42:53.530 --> 01:42:56.410
Bring the children to bed.
- Come. children.

730
01:42:56.529 --> 01:42:58.090
Daddy's tired. Go on.

731
01:43:00.209 --> 01:43:01.648
Bye.daddy.

732
01:43:06.407 --> 01:43:10.207
What happened?
- I was too late. I...

733
01:43:12.605 --> 01:43:14.286
Johan“.

734
01:43:31.481 --> 01:43:34.841
Gentlemen. look.
Cornelis De Witt's penis. Five cents.

735
01:43:34.960 --> 01:43:36.840
Piss off. man.

736
01:43:37.879 --> 01:43:39.560
Barbaric.

737
01:43:41.039 --> 01:43:43.438
It had to be done.

738
01:43:43.518 --> 01:43:46.679
They would've tried
to seize power again.

739
01:43:46.799 --> 01:43:49.157
We have to know who we can trust.

740
01:43:49.278 --> 01:43:54.237
We can't allow for Tromp
to serve under De Ruyter.

741
01:43:54.356 --> 01:43:56.915
I want to serve.
but not under De Ruyter.

742
01:43:57.076 --> 01:43:59.474
De Ruyter stays.

743
01:43:59.636 --> 01:44:03.554
I've appointed him for life.
and I'm a man of my word.

744
01:44:03.674 --> 01:44:05.313
Make it up with him.

745
01:44:09.752 --> 01:44:13.232
Old Tromp whispered something
to me before he died.

746
01:44:15.390 --> 01:44:20.270
About the way the wind blows. and that
an admiral has to keep his course.

747
01:44:22.110 --> 01:44:25.749
I thought he was talking nonsense.
but now I understand.

748
01:44:28.508 --> 01:44:29.667
Politics.

749
01:44:31.907 --> 01:44:34.667
Only one thing counts for an admiral.

750
01:44:36.586 --> 01:44:41.505
I've heard enough. You're going
to do what they ask of you.

751
01:44:42.864 --> 01:44:44.265
Go.

752
01:44:45.904 --> 01:44:49.103
Try to understand.
- They almost killed us too.

753
01:44:50.063 --> 01:44:51.383
I know.

754
01:44:56.143 --> 01:45:01.701
Promise me one thing. When all of this
is over. we go back to Vlissingen.

755
01:45:01.820 --> 01:45:03.499
You. me. the children.

756
01:45:07.340 --> 01:45:10.499
The army needs reinforcements here.

757
01:45:10.659 --> 01:45:15.178
The cities along the lJssel have
surrendered to the French.

758
01:45:15.297 --> 01:45:18.218
Let's turn the navy into land forces.

759
01:45:18.376 --> 01:45:20.376
Where can we cut the dikes?

760
01:45:25.574 --> 01:45:30.013
Your Highness. do you realize
what the consequences will be?

761
01:45:30.134 --> 01:45:33.493
Are you sure?
Thousands of people live there.

762
01:45:33.614 --> 01:45:37.333
All civilians. Your Highness.
- I want the exact locations.

763
01:45:38.771 --> 01:45:40.331
Leave us.

764
01:45:43.852 --> 01:45:45.290
You stay here.

765
01:45:48.291 --> 01:45:49.531
Admiral.

766
01:45:52.208 --> 01:45:54.008
Your Highness.

767
01:45:55.328 --> 01:45:58.048
I congratulate you
on your appointment.

768
01:46:00.647 --> 01:46:05.246
I know how you feel. De Ruyter.
- Do you?

769
01:46:06.726 --> 01:46:09.166
The French are nearing Amsterdam.

770
01:46:09.325 --> 01:46:13.164
The English will attack.
with the help of the French fleet.

771
01:46:17.483 --> 01:46:23.161
You have to make up with Tromp.
The country needs you. Both of you.

772
01:46:32.280 --> 01:46:34.039
I will follow your orders.

773
01:46:40.878 --> 01:46:42.477
I'm sure you will.

774
01:46:43.797 --> 01:46:45.236
You have my word.

775
01:46:45.356 --> 01:46:50.396
Well clone. Gentlemen. excuse me.
we're going to flood the country.

776
01:47:19.589 --> 01:47:21.909
Huzzah for De Ruyter and Tromp.

777
01:47:28.747 --> 01:47:30.387
Let's not overdo it.

778
01:47:44.023 --> 01:47:46.063
Let's get to work.

779
01:48:01.500 --> 01:48:05.219
Welcome. admiral.

780
01:48:15.737 --> 01:48:18.975
The English receive help
from the French fleet.

781
01:48:21.736 --> 01:48:24.254
You've already started.

782
01:48:24.374 --> 01:48:27.854
According to the latest updates
they're here and here.

783
01:48:27.974 --> 01:48:32.013
Not only do they want to destroy
our ships. but go ashore as well.

784
01:48:44.009 --> 01:48:47.809
The English want an invasion.
That's to our advantage.

785
01:48:47.969 --> 01:48:52.849
They want to reach the coast. so
they'll try to go ashore here or here.

786
01:49:02.966 --> 01:49:08.124
The wind comes from the south. and
so we'll do what they expect us to do.

787
01:49:08.245 --> 01:49:10.725
We're going to sail in line here...

788
01:49:10.844 --> 01:49:16.003
and then Tromp is going to leave
a hole here. He's good at that.

789
01:49:19.442 --> 01:49:25.240
You want them to sail through.
- The tide could be in our advantage.

790
01:49:25.361 --> 01:49:26.720
It's our only chance.

791
01:49:28.520 --> 01:49:30.479
Brilliant.

792
01:49:30.599 --> 01:49:35.439
My head is like an old piss bucket.
Can someone tell me what the plan is?

793
01:49:59.113 --> 01:50:01.432
Girls. you're going with Klaartje.

794
01:50:01.552 --> 01:50:04.752
You can't go to the coast by yourself.
- Go on.

795
01:50:06.671 --> 01:50:10.790
Not through the front door.
Through the back.

796
01:50:32.665 --> 01:50:35.345
Hoist the sails. Pull the ropes.

797
01:51:17.094 --> 01:51:19.254
Keep going.

798
01:51:19.534 --> 01:51:21.294
They're taking the bait.

799
01:51:42.969 --> 01:51:45.089
Come on.

800
01:51:55.206 --> 01:51:57.126
Everyone. get off the ship.

801
01:52:21.640 --> 01:52:24.240
We're going through that hole there.

802
01:52:26.119 --> 01:52:28.399
It's our chance to reach the coast.

803
01:52:31.238 --> 01:52:33.518
Man the guns.

804
01:52:35.436 --> 01:52:38.477
Hurry up. prepare the cannons.

805
01:52:49.194 --> 01:52:53.114
For once I do what you say...
- Admiral. The French fleet arrived.

806
01:52:53.312 --> 01:52:55.512
Take the Vooruitgang.
You know the plan.

807
01:52:55.633 --> 01:52:57.593
Aye aye. admiral.

808
01:52:57.672 --> 01:53:00.632
Boatswains in front of the mast.

809
01:53:49.100 --> 01:53:51.379
Prepare to come about.

810
01:53:57.819 --> 01:53:59.619
Get ready.

811
01:53:59.739 --> 01:54:02.977
De Ruyter is trying to defend
the coast. Let's go.

812
01:54:33.290 --> 01:54:36.170
Damn it.

813
01:54:36.290 --> 01:54:38.288
Abandon ship.

814
01:54:49.607 --> 01:54:52.446
Let us come about then.

815
01:54:52.566 --> 01:54:56.205
Load starboard.

816
01:54:56.325 --> 01:54:58.324
Prepare to come about.

817
01:55:01.285 --> 01:55:02.524
Come about.

818
01:55:02.643 --> 01:55:05.723
Prepare to come about.

819
01:55:22.719 --> 01:55:24.599
Every ship should pull back.

820
01:55:24.878 --> 01:55:28.317
Lift those cannons. Up.

821
01:55:28.398 --> 01:55:30.397
Carpenters. to the front.

822
01:55:38.396 --> 01:55:40.595
Fire.

823
01:55:58.032 --> 01:56:00.150
Pull back.

824
01:56:01.471 --> 01:56:05.029
Pull back.

825
01:56:31.504 --> 01:56:33.622
To victory.

826
01:56:35.462 --> 01:56:38.382
Huzzah for De Ruyter.

827
01:56:42.340 --> 01:56:45.301
Bestevaer.

828
01:56:50.220 --> 01:56:54.379
Bestevaer.

829
01:57:13.893 --> 01:57:18.252
You know what you promised.
- Just one more talk and it's over.

830
01:57:18.333 --> 01:57:20.333
People are being arrested everywhere.

831
01:57:20.452 --> 01:57:23.891
Don't say anything foolish
to the Prince.

832
01:57:24.052 --> 01:57:27.850
There are some people here
I want to introduce you to.

833
01:57:27.970 --> 01:57:32.210
These gentleman represent
about a quarter of our army.

834
01:57:32.329 --> 01:57:34.329
You want me to join a rebellion?

835
01:57:34.408 --> 01:57:39.608
You can be the symbol of our
resistance. The people look up to you.

836
01:57:39.727 --> 01:57:43.407
And I have the fleet behind me.
You're crazy. man.

837
01:57:43.526 --> 01:57:45.926
Plunge the country into a civil war?

838
01:57:46.686 --> 01:57:50.845
Anything is better
than a dictatorship.

839
01:57:54.005 --> 01:57:57.044
A disgrace.
This is a total disgrace.

840
01:57:57.484 --> 01:58:00.482
Be careful. Michiel.
Trust no one.

841
01:58:16.319 --> 01:58:17.680
Look around you.

842
01:58:17.800 --> 01:58:21.519
That just gives
them a reason to arrest you.

843
01:58:21.638 --> 01:58:25.198
We have to show
that we can work together.

844
01:58:26.198 --> 01:58:28.796
We must rebuild this country together.

845
01:58:46.272 --> 01:58:50.951
The republicans are reorganizing.
- They want De Ruyter as their leader.

846
01:58:51.071 --> 01:58:55.911
The people love him.
- That's the problem. Your Highness.

847
01:58:56.030 --> 01:58:58.310
We have a plan to solve that problem.

848
01:59:06.828 --> 01:59:08.947
The Prince of Orange.

849
01:59:26.463 --> 01:59:27.823
Thank you.

850
01:59:31.783 --> 01:59:34.421
I would like to thank one man...

851
01:59:34.501 --> 01:59:39.740
without whom this glorious victory
would never have occurred.

852
01:59:39.900 --> 01:59:43.219
The great hero
from the Battle of Texel:

853
01:59:43.340 --> 01:59:44.779
Cornelis Tromp.

854
01:59:49.018 --> 01:59:51.377
They don't know what they're doing.

855
02:00:08.055 --> 02:00:09.413
Bravo.

856
02:00:11.453 --> 02:00:12.734
Bravo.

857
02:00:37.927 --> 02:00:40.966
Do you have a moment?
I'll be right with you.

858
02:00:53.324 --> 02:00:56.764
Retirement?
Back to Zeeland?

859
02:00:56.883 --> 02:00:59.643
What will the Netherlands do
without you?

860
02:00:59.762 --> 02:01:02.682
This country has a great leader.

861
02:01:02.801 --> 02:01:05.000
The country has a great leader.

862
02:01:05.121 --> 02:01:08.080
How can I be a great leader
for all the Dutch...

863
02:01:08.199 --> 02:01:12.039
if they don't all love me?
I'm not like him.

864
02:01:12.999 --> 02:01:16.079
Your Highness
is underestimating himself.

865
02:01:17.278 --> 02:01:18.238
Are you serious?

866
02:01:18.359 --> 02:01:23.476
The king can unite the country.
Rise above the parties.

867
02:01:23.637 --> 02:01:27.036
You want me to release the rebels.
- A nice gesture.

868
02:01:27.117 --> 02:01:29.636
Have you heard
what they say about me?

869
02:01:29.715 --> 02:01:34.195
That's how they thank me.
after everything I did for my people.

870
02:01:34.315 --> 02:01:36.474
Surely you can admit that.

871
02:01:37.193 --> 02:01:40.912
Should I just watch the republicans
ruin our country?

872
02:01:41.032 --> 02:01:42.832
I can't just stand idly by.

873
02:01:42.953 --> 02:01:45.671
Like with Johan and Cornelis de Witt?

874
02:01:45.832 --> 02:01:49.231
Was that massacre also
for the good of the country?

875
02:01:49.390 --> 02:01:52.790
I had nothing...
- Nothing to do with that?

876
02:01:55.269 --> 02:01:58.549
We couldn't control the mob.
No one had any idea.

877
02:01:58.669 --> 02:02:01.867
Your people incited the nation
against the De Witts for months.

878
02:02:02.827 --> 02:02:06.987
Pamphlets. agitators.
filthy back room politics.

879
02:02:07.067 --> 02:02:08.906
How dare you?

880
02:02:09.025 --> 02:02:12.306
You'll have to live
with your conscience.

881
02:02:12.465 --> 02:02:15.145
How dare you?

882
02:02:15.944 --> 02:02:18.264
Still De Witt's friend. eh?

883
02:02:18.383 --> 02:02:21.664
I'm starting to doubt
if you'll obey me when it's needed.

884
02:02:21.784 --> 02:02:24.224
I have always served my country.

885
02:02:24.343 --> 02:02:27.222
If only the country
was as stable as you.

886
02:02:28.182 --> 02:02:31.340
Your Highness can be assured
of my dedication.

887
02:02:36.660 --> 02:02:38.020
But am I?

888
02:02:59.015 --> 02:03:00.215
Admiral.

889
02:03:06.012 --> 02:03:09.932
I hoped this wouldn't be necessary.
but my advisers were right.

890
02:03:11.172 --> 02:03:14.131
I'll accept your retirement
on one condition.

891
02:03:15.131 --> 02:03:19.891
Your Highness?
- You carry out one last mission.

892
02:03:20.010 --> 02:03:25.170
You're going to the Mediterranean Sea.
- A secret mission against the French.

893
02:03:25.328 --> 02:03:26.928
Why should I?

894
02:03:27.009 --> 02:03:30.567
It's not wise to refuse a direct order
from your Prince.

895
02:03:32.247 --> 02:03:35.326
It's hard to protect
a traitor's family.

896
02:03:41.284 --> 02:03:42.524
De Ruyter.

897
02:04:04.200 --> 02:04:09.598
I might as well have condemned him to
death. That would've been more honest.

898
02:04:09.718 --> 02:04:12.358
Think of it as an act
of a true statesman.

899
02:04:22.435 --> 02:04:25.914
I've decided to form an alliance
with the English throne.

900
02:04:27.275 --> 02:04:30.674
I have to seize this opportunity.

901
02:04:33.712 --> 02:04:36.152
A marriage with Mary Stuart.

902
02:04:40.911 --> 02:04:43.710
Think of it as an act
of a true statesman.

903
02:05:00.226 --> 02:05:01.906
I couldn't sleep either.

904
02:05:09.065 --> 02:05:10.785
Why. Michiel?

905
02:05:14.263 --> 02:05:16.583
Why did you accept that mission?

906
02:05:17.904 --> 02:05:20.183
You have nothing to prove.
They can't force us.

907
02:05:20.302 --> 02:05:22.102
That's not it.

908
02:05:22.343 --> 02:05:26.422
So you want a state funeral?
- I don't want to cause a civil war.

909
02:05:26.581 --> 02:05:30.660
And you won't. It's not your fault
those men are in prison.

910
02:05:30.781 --> 02:05:33.180
Someone has to obey the Prince.

911
02:05:33.300 --> 02:05:35.180
The Prince?

912
02:05:35.299 --> 02:05:39.539
He only wants to get rid of you.
They all want to get rid of you.

913
02:05:39.658 --> 02:05:43.656
Your success is too great.
Don't you see what they're doing?

914
02:05:43.776 --> 02:05:46.737
They want you dead.
just like with Johan.

915
02:05:46.856 --> 02:05:51.775
Someone needs to lead by example.
- A good example.

916
02:05:51.895 --> 02:05:55.294
Let someone else do it.
They always reconcile.

917
02:05:55.415 --> 02:05:58.934
Too much blood has been spilled.
The country is torn.

918
02:05:59.013 --> 02:06:01.934
I don't care if the country is torn.

919
02:06:02.013 --> 02:06:05.093
I just want us to enjoy
our retirement in peace.

920
02:06:06.972 --> 02:06:08.771
What do you mean?

921
02:06:17.409 --> 02:06:19.288
What did the Prince say?

922
02:06:20.288 --> 02:06:21.768
Did he threaten us?

923
02:06:23.967 --> 02:06:27.206
So he did.
- He wasn't even subtle about it.

924
02:06:27.288 --> 02:06:30.767
And you want to risk your life again
for a man like that?

925
02:06:31.765 --> 02:06:34.965
A man who has never cared
about other people...

926
02:06:35.046 --> 02:06:37.684
or what it's like for us
and the children.

927
02:06:37.804 --> 02:06:40.844
I do this for you and the children.

928
02:06:42.604 --> 02:06:45.802
He guarantees your safety
while I'm gone.

929
02:06:49.083 --> 02:06:51.561
And if you survive and come back?

930
02:06:53.481 --> 02:06:54.960
Will it be over then?

931
02:06:55.800 --> 02:06:57.680
Will they leave us alone?

932
02:07:02.759 --> 02:07:04.678
You're not coming back.

933
02:07:07.397 --> 02:07:10.638
You're not leaving me alone.
do you hear me?

934
02:07:11.957 --> 02:07:14.236
You're not leaving me by myself.

935
02:07:15.157 --> 02:07:19.675
Of course. darling.
Of course I'm coming back.

936
02:07:26.233 --> 02:07:27.594
No. no. no. no.

937
02:07:37.631 --> 02:07:39.230
Be a good boy.

938
02:07:40.151 --> 02:07:46.950
Raise up. Smooth.

939
02:07:54.267 --> 02:07:56.308
Daddy loves you very much.

940
02:08:01.865 --> 02:08:03.345
Forgive me. my love.

941
02:08:40.017 --> 02:08:41.856
Come on. let's go home.

942
02:09:26.086 --> 02:09:29.486
I count no more than 12 ships.
Where is the Seven Provinces?

943
02:09:34.045 --> 02:09:37.205
Is that all they have?
What's the honour in that?

944
02:09:44.602 --> 02:09:47.842
Prepare for combat.
- Get ready.

945
02:10:24.553 --> 02:10:27.752
Load the cannons.

946
02:10:43.669 --> 02:10:45.747
Fire.

947
02:10:56.346 --> 02:10:58.226
Reload the cannons.

948
02:11:12.862 --> 02:11:14.742
Hurry up with those cannons.

949
02:11:24.179 --> 02:11:25.739
God damn it.

950
02:11:40.855 --> 02:11:42.974
Faster. faster.

951
02:12:59.877 --> 02:13:35.109
Fire.

952
02:13:35.109 --> 02:13:37.268
Surgeon to the top deck.

953
02:13:40.229 --> 02:13:41.987
Stay with us.

954
02:13:42.667 --> 02:13:45.466
Slightly more to port.

955
02:13:47.787 --> 02:13:49.107
Anna.

956
02:14:16.860 --> 02:14:19.100
Michiel de Ruyter is dead.

957
02:14:20.579 --> 02:14:25.137
Load the cannons with blank shells.
Let's honour our enemy.

958
02:14:25.258 --> 02:14:27.937
Get ready to pay tribute.

959
02:15:56.916 --> 02:15:59.396
Look at them.

960
02:15:59.476 --> 02:16:03.676
Orangists and republicans.
side by side for the first time.

961
02:16:08.474 --> 02:16:10.274
I never could have done that.

962
02:16:22.471 --> 02:16:24.150
I've seen enough.

963
02:16:28.710 --> 02:16:30.469
The end of an era.

964
02:16:31.749 --> 02:16:33.989
That is Anna De Ruyter.
let her through.

965
02:16:56.703 --> 02:17:01.143
Give him the most beautiful grave
possible.

966
02:17:03.261 --> 02:17:04.582
All right.

967
02:17:05.802 --> 02:17:11.761
